      "narration": {
        "text": "Gross domestic product, or GDP, is the total value of output of goods and services in a country in one year. Economic growth is when real GDP increases. A recession is falling GDP, usually two consecutive quarters of negative growth. Brambledon watches these figures before planning stock. If GDP falls for two quarters, the firm delays its new frame line.",
