      "narration": {
        "text": "Fiscal policy uses taxation and public spending to influence demand. Corporation tax comes out of retained profit, leaving less for Brambledon to invest. Higher income tax cuts disposable income, so customers buy fewer bikes. More government spending can create orders, or compete for scarce resources and push costs up. A lower tax rate leaves more cash, but the government then collects less to spend on services.",
