      "narration": {
        "text": "On one side, lower rates and lower taxes lift demand and profit. Brambledon can hire and expand. On the other side, cheap credit can fuel inflation, and rate rises make loans expensive. Higher taxes reduce profit but fund services that support demand. Which lever matters most depends on whether the problem is weak sales or rising costs. A boom needs cooling, while a slump needs stimulus, so policy must match the stage of the cycle we are in.",
