        "text": "Time to apply this. Imagine interest rates rise and income tax falls at the same time. Which effect hits Brambledon first, and which is more significant for a firm with a large loan? On screen, two levers move in opposite directions. Choose your answer, then watch the arrows show the result. A larger loan means heavier repayments, so the rate rise usually bites harder than extra spending power from tax in the short run for this business.",
